    "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen a test imports PyTorch's internal test helpers, cuDNN flags become frozen. Main's process-state fixtures then raise during teardown while restoring settings, even when the test itself passes.\n\nRelated main attention output-gate PR: #8008.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Restore captured cuDNN settings through the flag setter used by PyTorch's own context manager.\n- Preserve the frozen policy and uncaptured enabled, benchmark-limit, and precision settings, with compatibility for versions lacking the precision argument.\n- Add real locked/unlocked and changed/unchanged restoration regressions.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Canonical unit-test runner on 8 H100 GPUs: all ranks passed the four new regression cases with no failures or skips.\n- The original main restoration function reproduces the frozen-flags error in the same environment.\n- Official main autoformat checks passed Black, isort, Pylint, and Ruff.\n\nValidation used the cached CI-derived Torch 26.04 environment, not a fresh install from main's current lockfile. This infrastructure fix is kept separate from the attention output-gate feature.\n",
